From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Euclid Ye <yezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:58:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport: deps: Update url to 2.5.9 to fix vulnerability
 (#50138)

Stack overflow in `Url::origin()` on nested `blob:` URLs. See
[RUSTSEC-2026-0592](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0592.html)
This is patched in 2.5.9.

Testing: It builds.

---------

Signed-off-by: Euclid Ye <yezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit d22050dbbf0d5d7544df2f2a77bea18c4038a027)

----

Fork note: backported onto Servo v0.6.0 for the ohos-v0.6 branch. cargo-deny in test-tidy reports RUSTSEC-2026-0592 (url 2.5.8, stack overflow in Url::origin on nested blob: URLs) for v0.6.0's lock file. Cargo.lock takes only the url and form_urlencoded crates: the change of one crate's syn dependency to 3.0.4 that came along upstream is left out, because v0.6.0 resolves that crate with syn 2.

Validation: On the final stack, at its tip: `./mach test-tidy` (including cargo-deny), `./mach test-scripts`, `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, the crown build (checked-release, -D warnings, crown built for Rust 1.97.1), `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` with and without `--doc`, and the OpenHarmony checked-release builds of both flavors with -D warnings, which make signed HAPs, pass; release builds of it with both engines ran the whole WPT suite. The 77 url tests run as expected with both engines with the expectations this commit removes; cargo-deny no longer reports RUSTSEC-2026-0592.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked upstream commit d22050dbbf0, left its syn change out of Cargo.lock and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
